 person  only wants to speak to the hand Allison  is on hand as the silent sisters prepare  viserys's body to be burned she puts his  crown on his chest and cries over his  body he may not have been the husband  that she dreamed of but it is clear in  this moment that she cared for him  deeply she then goes to meet with  rainey's which is probably the most  gripping Exchange in the episode Allison  lays out all the heartache that has come  come on house valarian as a result of  their loyalty to rhaenyra and Damon she  makes a decent case from her point of  view and the most notable thing she says  is that as women they don't rule but  they can try to guide the men that do  gently I think this is the takeaway  we're supposed to have about Alison as a  character at this point if you think  back to the green Council it wouldn't  really make sense that she was surprised  that they were thinking about putting  aegon on the throne as I mentioned this  is something that Otto's been talking  about since aegon was born and until  viserys's speech at dinner this is  something that she was actively trying  to do I think what the show is going for  is that it's not that she doesn't want  that to happen even though she may have  been wavering on her position after the  rape incident in the last episode but  she wanted to do it without the violence  her main issue here is not that he's  going to be king it's that Otto wants to  kill rhaenyra the subtext for the  conversation that she's having with  rhaenys though is that they need need  her dragon and for this she's willing to  offer her drift Mark for her and her  granddaughters to do with as they see  fit rainey's acknowledges that she's a  little smarter than she thought she was  but crushes her justification by saying  and yet you toil yourself in service to  men your father your husband your son  you desire not to be free but to make a  window in the wall of your prison have  you never imagined yourself on the Iron  Throne these are things that Alison has  no response for and she leaves her there  to think about her offer Kristen and  emancy auto meeting with mazaria she  knows that the king is dead and reveals  she's hidden aegon away somewhere safe  she'll tell them where he is if they'll  pay her and agree to stop the kid fights  we saw happening in flea bottom she  directs them to the hiding place in the  sept where aegon makes it clear that he  doesn't want to be found when they take  him outside Cole and Eamon are there to  try to intercept them they want to take  him to the queen a fight breaks out and  Eric with an e the one who's been making  the case that this is not the person  that he wants to see as King of the  Seven Kingdoms sort of sits it out and  then at the end we see him slip away  when Eamon gets a hold of aegon he asks  him to let him go and says he'll  disappear and you see that Eamonn  understands that this could lead to him  becoming the King instead but Kristen  intervenes and takes him to his mother  and I didn't mention it earlier but  Eamon says he's next in line which he  should know isn't actually the case if  the firstborn were to die then it would  follow his line and since he does have  that air I mentioned earlier jaharis  would have a better claim than Eamonn I  trust that the writers understand this  so I wonder what it is that they're  trying to say about this character  Alison does win the race to secure aegon  and that means that she's in charge of  putting together the Ascension in defeat  Otto says whatever our differences our  hearts remain as one and Allison quickly  refutes this saying I see now that I was  just a piece you moved around the board  while this doesn't bode well for their  relationship after she declares that a  reluctance to murder is not a weakness  she quickly pivots to laying out her  plan for how things will go down they'll  send terms to rhaenyra True terms that  she can accept aegon will be crowned by  a septon in the morning wearing the  crown of the Conqueror and carrying his  sword blackfyre they'll use every symbol  they have at their disposal to help  people remember the ancient strength of  House Targaryen they'll do it as a  dragon pit and everyone in King's  Landing will have to be there to witness  it and this does show an understanding  of what their advantage is this  proximity to the actual Iron Throne if  they can get him crowned in front of  enough people they can make them believe  that he is the king Otto still argues  that if rhaenyra is allowed to live then  people will put their banners behind her  until she returns and this is something  that I'll come back to because I do  think he's right to some extent but I  don't get why he thinks killing her  would solve that problem and not getting  what he wants it's clear that just like  when she pulled the dagger on rhaenyra  he's into seeing this side of his  daughter and even adds the comment that  she resembles her mother in certain  lights to drive that home she returns to  her room where she finds Laris waiting  for her he's found out something that  she should know and before you can even  realize what's going on they enter into  this negotiation he asked if she  wondered how her father found aegon  first to this she sits down on the couch  and without anyone saying anything she  takes off her shoes and presents her  feet for him to see he explains to her  that there is a web of spies in the  castle which he probably found out about  when Talia was in the cells and maybe  more importantly that her father knows  about it he pauses before he reveals  more so that she can remove her  stockings then he tells her about Talia  and lays out a plan that if he kills the  leader then Otto will lose his advantage  and of course this is something that he  can do if she Wills him to she then  begrudgingly puts her feet up on the  couch and turns away while he rubs one  out by the look on her face we can see  that this is not something she does for  fun this isn't sex play that they both  take part in because they find it  mutually satisfying this is the price  that she pays to get this information  it's a little on the nose but I guess it  makes some sense that given his  condition he might have a thing for  healthy feet but what stood out most to  me about this was how routine it all  seemed this is definitely not the first  time they've done it and it's notable  that she knows what she's asking him to  do here and is willing to be complicit  in Murder because he suggested it and  it's not something that she wants to  know more about there's definitely been  some Evolution since the last time they  had one of these kind of conversations  and while I do think that this is his  thing I think there is more to it based  on the fact that she's such a powerful  woman that he can make do this sir which  I only know because I know which one  ends up wearing the book bust into  Princess rainey's room to help her  Escape he's decided that he can't get  behind the crowning of aegon and leads  her out of the red keep on the way out  they passed Lord caswell's body we saw  him get caught on his way out earlier  and now he's hanging there as a  deterrent to anyone else who might think  about following rhaenyra we also see  mazaria's house burning down and a man  in a cloak walking away you can't really  see who this is but I'm assuming this is  one of his tongueless assassins because  it lingered on his Cane with the Firefly  and when you look at this scene closely  you can see what looks like that same  pin Eric is trying to get rhaenys to a  boat on the river and she's worried  about leaving melees behind as they're  walking they run into the crowds of  people the city watch is hurting towards  the coronation she gets caught in the  crowd and has to move in the same  direction as Alison is accompanying  aegon on the way to his coronation he  points out the obvious his father never  wanted him to be king he didn't even  really like him he had 20 years to make  that decision and he stood by his choice  of rhaenyra he laughs at the idea that  with his final breath he changed his  mind because to be fair it is kind of  laughable and to that she offers him his  namesake's dagger and you can see the  idea starting to set in for him rhaenys  is relieved to realize that the crowd is  being led to the dragon pit when she  makes her way inside we hear Otto  addressing the crowd he tells them that  viserys the peaceful is dead and in his  final moments he declared that his  firstborn son aegon should succeed him  the ceremony is put together really well  and the actor does a fantastic job in  showing the range of emotions he  experiences as he realizes that even  though this is something that he didn't  want there are much worse things than  being the king when the crowd starts to  cheer and he and she's his House's  ancestral Valerian steel blade you can  see that he's very much into it not that  long ago he woke up under a table in the  sept after a night out whoring and now  he's the most powerful man in the Seven  Kingdoms while this was all going on  rainey's had slipped away and reunited  with her Dragon melees they burst out of  the floor from the lower level and  Scattered the crowd killing at least  hundreds maybe even thousands of them  she's right there in front of the  usurpers they have a stare down where  Allison puts herself in front of the  king and rainey's opts not to give the  commander Karis to burn them instead she  flies away which is amazing looking and  the episode cuts to Black this was a  strange episode which in my mind is a  step down from the last two in a lot of  ways but at the same time some of the  performances were so good that they  overshadowed a lot of the problems I had  I still don't love that a  misunderstanding pushed Alison and over  the edge to get behind aegon but Olivia  Cook delivered so many great moments in  the process of showing how that happened  the episode did work to make the  character more sympathetic in the way  that the previous two did for rhaenyra  and I do think that will probably  increase watchability as things develop  they did a good job of portraying aegon  as awful and unfit to rule while still  giving us some insight into why he  behaves the way he does and as I've  already mentioned Tom Glenn Carney  really showed up for the coronation  scene I also like how there doesn't seem  to be that same love between him and  Eamon as there was with viserys and his  brother which is one of Damon's only  redeemable qualities aegon is a rough  sell for everyone involved including his  mother who has now committed her life to  making sure that he remains in power and  I don't think that we're supposed to  think that gently guiding him is what  this situation calls for I think whether  you like this episode or not will come  down to whether you like the closing set  piece with rhaenys and melees and I  think that's kind of a shame I thought  that it looked great but it also felt  like it only existed because they wanted  to have something major happen in the  closing scene of this penultimate  episode the conversation she had with  Allison was so good and this didn't  necessarily seem like it matched up with  what they were saying I suppose they  were going for the idea that she doesn't  want to escalate the situation like she  has the power to wipe them out which we  know would save a lot of lives and I  know a lot of people are saying that she  didn't want to be a kin Slayer but  they're actively usurping the throne  from your other kin and she did Kill  quite a few of the small folk which I  know is completely consistent with the  way the targaryens think about them but  I feel like this is supposed to be this  dramatic event where she turns the other  cheek or whatever and it just didn't  really land for me also Auto is awful  but he has been portrayed as smart and  careful in the book he takes several  days to methodically set up a situation  that will make the blacks look like the  bad guys no matter how they respond to  it and here he just seemed like a garden  variety bad guy he mentions that her  supporters will call their banners to  get behind her and that's the same  reason why killing her doesn't make a  lot of sense yeah there's no immediate  error there if they kill her and  exterminate her whole family but I don't  think they set it up as a situation  where he thought that he would be able  to get away with that without any  consequences but hey you know what this  is only one side of the story so I do  like that we didn't see the reaction yet  and some of this might make more sense  when we see how that plays out  stylistically I thought it was a great  looking episode I thought the score  added a lot to some of the quiet scenes  and some of the conversations and  overall I think that it may not have  been as good as what we've seen scene  but I'm not exactly worried I'm still  looking forward to see what happens next  and I think that's a great place to  leave things let me know in the comments  what you thought about this episode and  how you feel going into the finale  please like this video If you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  I'll talk to you soon
 

